# SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
# Bustfile — failure mode contractile for boj-server-cartridges
# Author: Jonathan D.A. Jewell <j.d.a.jewell@open.ac.uk>
#
# Paired runner: bust.ncl
# Verb:          bust
# Semantics:     Every declared failure mode must have a working recovery path
#                that has been exercised. Status moves:
#                  declared → drilled (probe run) → verified (recovery confirmed)
#                  or → failing (recovery broken)
#
# CLI:
#   contractile bust check  → list failure modes + recovery status
#   contractile bust drill  → inject failures, verify recovery paths
#
# Rewritten 2026-08-07. The previous version had this repository's name
# substituted in but still described it as "the canonical template for RSR
# compliance", with failure modes about template distribution. It is not a
# template. It is the sole source of BoJ cartridges for every host.

[metadata]
project = "boj-server-cartridges"
version = "0.2.0"
last-updated = "2026-08-07"

@abstract:
Failure modes for boj-server-cartridges, the canonical registry of BoJ
capability cartridges.

Since hyperpolymath/boj-server#300 merged (2026-08-04) no host carries a
bundled fallback tree, so every failure mode below has a blast radius of
"every BoJ host on its next fetch". None of these has been drilled; status
is recorded honestly as `declared` rather than assumed working.
@end

## Failure Modes

### schema-mirror-drift
- class: supply_chain
- description: schemas/cartridge-v1.json silently diverges from the upstream it mirrors, so manifests validate against a schema nobody approved
- injection_probe: "printf '\\n' >> schemas/cartridge-v1.json"
- recovery_probe: "test \"$(sha256sum schemas/cartridge-v1.json | awk '{print $1}')\" != \"$(awk -F'\\\"' '/content_sha256/ {print $2}' schemas/PINNED-SHA)\" && git checkout schemas/cartridge-v1.json"
- expected_recovery_time_seconds: 5
- status: declared
- notes: The detection half of this is REAL and runs in CI (cartridge-schema re-verifies the content SHA-256 before validating). The recovery half is a manual git checkout. Drilling it means confirming the CI job actually goes red, not just that the local test does.

### invalid-manifest-reaches-main
- class: registry_integrity
- description: A cartridge.json that does not validate lands on main and every host fetches it
- injection_probe: "cd tools/validate-cartridges && deno task strict"
- recovery_probe: "git revert --no-edit HEAD"
- expected_recovery_time_seconds: 300
- status: declared
- notes: Prevention is strong (strict gate since 2026-06-01, 142/142). Recovery is weak: there is no host-side pin, so a bad merge propagates on the next fetch and the only rollback is another merge. A host-side ref pin would change this failure mode's severity materially.

### template-defect-propagates
- class: amplification
- description: A defect in cartridges/templates/gossamer-mcp/ is copied into every subsequently minted cartridge
- injection_probe: "grep -rn 'gossamer_init' cartridges/templates/gossamer-mcp/adapter/"
- recovery_probe: "cd cartridges/templates/gossamer-mcp/adapter && zig build"
- expected_recovery_time_seconds: 3600
- status: failing
- notes: NOT HYPOTHETICAL — THIS HAS ALREADY HAPPENED. The template adapter calls ffi.gossamer_init, which does not exist, and the ffi `export fn` declarations are not `pub`. All 99 adapter/build.zig trees inherit the fault and none of them compiles. Recovery requires fixing the template and then re-propagating to 99 cartridges. Status is `failing`, not `declared`, because the recovery path is known-broken today.

### silent-cartridge-rot
- class: coverage
- description: A cartridge stops building and nothing notices, because CI only builds what a PR touched
- injection_probe: "grep -c 'cartridges/.*/ffi/' .github/workflows/zig-test.yml"
- recovery_probe: "for b in $(find cartridges -path '*/ffi/build.zig'); do (cd $(dirname $b) && zig build test) || echo FAIL $b; done"
- expected_recovery_time_seconds: 7200
- status: failing
- notes: The detection path does not exist on main. zig-test.yml filters on '^cartridges/.*/ffi/' and there is no scheduled full-tree sweep, so a cartridge nobody edits can rot indefinitely. Open PR #109 proposes a weekly full-sweep job. Until it merges the recovery probe above is the only sweep there is, and it is manual.

### shim-divergence
- class: vendored_copy
- description: One of the 116 vendored cartridge_shim.zig copies drifts from the template and the affected cartridge builds differently from every other
- injection_probe: "canon=$(sha256sum cartridges/templates/gossamer-mcp/ffi/cartridge_shim.zig | awk '{print $1}'); find cartridges -name cartridge_shim.zig -exec sha256sum {} \\; | grep -v \"^$canon\""
- recovery_probe: "cp cartridges/templates/gossamer-mcp/ffi/cartridge_shim.zig <divergent-path>"
- expected_recovery_time_seconds: 60
- status: failing
- notes: ALREADY OCCURRED. cartridges/domains/gaming/npc-mcp/ffi/cartridge_shim.zig differs from the canonical bytes and no record explains why. Do not run the recovery probe blind — establish first whether the divergence was intentional.

### proof-rot
- class: verification
- description: Idris2 ABI proofs stop type-checking while the board stays green
- injection_probe: "bash scripts/typecheck-proofs.sh"
- recovery_probe: "bash scripts/check-trusted-base.sh && bash scripts/typecheck-proofs.sh"
- expected_recovery_time_seconds: 1800
- status: drilled
- notes: This one HAS been exercised. 23 proofs here had rotted while their boj-server twins stayed green (#36/#37); the Proofs Gate was added in response and now type-checks every .idr individually with a vacuous-pass guard. Marked `drilled` rather than `verified` because the recovery was a one-off remediation, not a repeatable drill.

### contractile-parse-error
- class: contractile_format
- description: A contractile or 6a2 file fails to parse, so agents read no policy at all
- injection_probe: "printf 'invalid syntax\\n' >> .machine_readable/contractiles/Intentfile.a2ml"
- recovery_probe: "git checkout .machine_readable/contractiles/Intentfile.a2ml"
- expected_recovery_time_seconds: 5
- status: declared
- notes: There is no a2ml validator in this repository and no CI job parses these files, so the failure is silent by construction. The nearest thing to a check is that 0-AI-MANIFEST.a2ml happens to parse as YAML.
